{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs36 Communications\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The axis communication settings can be updated and saved to NVRAM in the motion controller. Once updated, the connection will be closed and you will need to {\i Initialize & Home All}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The axis must be de-energized before the communication settings can be edited and written to NVRAM. i.e.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\pict\pngblip\picw512\pich145\picwgoal6195\pichgoal1754\bin }\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 If the baud rate and/or address are changed, the configuration settings in {\i Instrument.cfg} will be updated automatically to match).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 If the communications protocol is changed (e.g. RS232 -> CAN), you will need to perform a 'Reconfigure' to update the configuration settings in {\i Instrument.cfg}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs32 Selecting the Communications Protocol\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 While you can configure the communication settings through the {\i MotionSynergyGUI}, to switch between RS232 Serial, RS485 Serial or CAN communications, you will need to set a series of dipswitches on the device itself.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\pict\pngblip\picw767\pich221\picwgoal9281\pichgoal2674\bin }\par}
}